{"ts":"2026-09-06T18:05:53.711Z","author":"codex","author_source":"configured","agent_harness":"codex","agent_model":"gpt-6-astra","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"a2704b943b957b3a91ea19fe","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"gpt-6-astra","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"medium","source":"probe"},"role":null,"topic":null},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments/1","value":{"created_at":"2026-09-06T18:05:53.711Z","author":"codex","text":"TDD evidence: the new real-process regression failed against the inherited-output wrapper because the delegated writer was still active when the outer 16-byte capture returned ENOBUFS. No filesystem errors or process results were mocked. The corrected wrapper captures its child output until exit before forwarding it, so the same regression can require the completion marker and ESRCH for the reaped PID. Negative fixtures now inherit a disposable global tracker and explicit Sentry/telemetry opt-outs before SDK imports."}},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-09-06T18:05:53.711Z"}],"before_hash":"8ba7929869fc838ed89269a2f2f74936aba440e2197c027af6546be8d55ee34d","after_hash":"c9ca43029138d931804327cca17b98605166a3f684ab2ca99fa8e0d2e99b7ca2","item_hash_version":3,"context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"version":{"status":"unavailable","reason":"harness_unavailable","resolver":"ai_agent_version","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"a4a7185f5d1ed43d42c47947951975d9dfe6b4c77f78658bcdbeee2b36ca6e23"}
{"ts":"2026-09-06T18:09:41.482Z","author":"codex","author_source":"configured","agent_harness":"codex","agent_model":"gpt-6-astra","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"a2704b943b957b3a91ea19fe","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"gpt-6-astra","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"medium","source":"probe"},"role":{"value":"implementer","source":"argv"},"topic":null},"op":"update","patch":[{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-09-06T18:09:41.482Z"},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/description","value":"The original ENOTEMPTY cleanup retry is shipped, but it does not establish writer lifetime. spawnSync waits for its direct child; when that child is the transparent test wrapper, a tiny outer output cap can kill the wrapper while its real pm descendant continues closing an item. Removing the temporary tracker can then race a history open and report an unintended CI fault through production observability. A real-process regression reproduces the surviving descendant. The corrected wrapper waits for real pm to exit before forwarding bounded captured output, and negative subprocess fixtures use an isolated global tracker with explicit observability opt-outs. The cleanup retry remains bounded for transient removal faults and its documentation now distinguishes child reaping from directory removal."},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/title","value":"Test wrapper lets delegated writers outlive buffer-overrun teardown"}],"before_hash":"c9ca43029138d931804327cca17b98605166a3f684ab2ca99fa8e0d2e99b7ca2","after_hash":"a872a3f361195f1ec87c82bfd0d8fafc83f24d2994128e15ed36784fe6e54fa8","item_hash_version":3,"message":"Correct the causal explanation using the real delegated-writer regression","context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"version":{"status":"unavailable","reason":"harness_unavailable","resolver":"ai_agent_version","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"50d07ddcecb5b427a99cfc96c9a61e9c3ba9d6